	(text "The ColecoVision cartridge port (MAME bus/coleco/cartridge/exp.h, ADAM Technical Reference Manual J1): even pins on\nthe component face, odd pins behind them.  A0-A14 and D0-D7 straight from the Z80; /8000 /A000 /C000 /E000 from the\nconsole's '138 (enabled by /MREQ and RFSH: a write selects as a read does).  No /RD, /WR, A15, clock or reset.\nA0-A14 reach GP0-14 through 330R (5 V-tolerant pads).  D0-D7 pass the 74LVC245A, whose /OE is the AND of the four\nselects: core1 drives GP15-22 off the bare address on every cycle (coleco_cart.c), and only a cart select lets the\nbyte onto the bus.  DIR (GP27, 1 = console -> cart, pulled up through reset) turns it round for the bank-register\nwrites; /CE (GP26) tells core1 the cycle is the cart's.  GP28 senses the console 5 V (10k / 15k = 3.0 V); GP25 the\nLED; GP23 / GP24 (UART1 TX) / GP29 bring-up pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "319f437e-3cc0-5794-be4b-3e80db62268d")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
